 "template": "In Odoo, open the Sales app and create a new quotation (New Quotation). Set the Customer to \"{{v1}}\" — the customer field is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually click the matching option from the dropdown that appears; a typed-only value does not count. Then add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again the product field is an autocomplete dropdown — type and click a real option from the dropdown), and set the quantity to 3. Let Odoo fill in the unit price automatically. Do NOT confirm the quotation yet — leave it as a draft quotation. Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price Odoo filled in on the line, (c) the untaxed amount (Untaxed Amount) the app computes in the totals, and (d) the quotation reference/name (e.g. S00042) shown on the record. Note: the app long-polls, so never wait for network idle; wait for concrete page state instead.",
